CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ A under construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ M under construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ after construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
During A's constructor the call reached M::id: only the complete object's
direct bases with virtual bases got construction vtables (Itanium C++ ABI
2.6.2), and M's base-object constructor left the tables its caller had
installed.  M's base-object constructor now builds A's tables from the
pointers in place: a copy of A's own tables with the virtual-base offsets
of the complete object (the ABI passes a VTT for this).
